     {
      "hitHighlights": {
       "dc.description.abstract": [
        "Summary of The Delhi Special Police Establishment <em>Act</em>, 1946,\nKey Provisions\nConstitution and Powers\n1.\tEstablishment Clause: - Formation: Establishment of the Delhi Special Police Establishment (DSPE) by the Central Government.\n•\tPrimary Function: Investigation of corruption and other notified offences in Union territories.\n•\tPowers of Members: Equipped with powers akin to local police for investigating specified offences.\n",
        "Superintendence and Administration: - Corruption Cases: Oversight by the Central Vigilance Commission (CVC) for Prevention of Corruption <em>Act</em> offences.\n•\tGeneral Matters: Superintendence by the Central Government.\n•\tDirector’s Role: Appointed by the Central Government, exercises powers similar to an Inspector-General of Police.\n3.\t"
       ],
       "dc.title": [
        "The Delhi Special Police Establishment <em>Act</em>, 1946"
       ]
